[A Hunter] At [TAR352 Dungar Longdrink] on the gate ramp, |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Menethil Harbor]|r (the game routes it through Ironforge; the hunter has no reason to stop there) [G71.0,72.5 Stormwind City]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffIronforge|r  -  the level-28 spells are the only reason for the tram
[A Shaman] Take the Deeprun Tram in the Dwarven District to Ironforge [G73.8,49.2 Stormwind City]
[A Shaman] In the Forlorn Cavern at [TAR258098 Eldrun Stormbreaker], [T] train your level 28 spells [G46.6,13.4 Ironforge]
[OC][A Shaman] Klockmort's Essential Artificials (2924, 3,050 XP) has no prerequisite in the DB, but its items are Artificial Extrapolators inside Gnomeregan: leave it for Tinkertown in chapter 24, which picks it up with its Darnassus breadcrumb (2925)
[A Shaman] At the flight master [TAR1573 Gryth Thurden], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Menethil Harbor]|r [G55.5,47.7 Ironforge]

[OC]|cffffffffMenethil Harbor|r  -  you land by the harbor and every pickup in this loop is within 12 units of it. Human hunters: Wowhead lists Bloom of the Heavens (98208, 98209), From the Ashes (98221), Crocs of the Sky (98072) and Highland Hides (98815) as not offered to Humans - if the NPC does not offer one, skip the line. Caitlin Grassman (11.9,58.8) has nothing for you yet: Lost in the Thicket Things (95647) needs Seeking Caitlin from Astranaar first (chapter 22).
At [TAR1217 Glorin Steelbrow] by the harbor, [QT270] [QA321 Lightforge Iron] (the wreck of the Flying Osprey is a short walk south) [G10.6,60.6 Wetlands]
[O]|cffffcc00Fish to 130+ / trout stock:|r you are 28 and the Mithril Head Trout buff (+20 attack power) has been usable since 25 - if you still cannot cook it, the gap is Cooking 175, not fish. Fish off the Menethil dock (Strong Pole + Nightcrawler; [TAR3178 Stuart Fleming] at 8.0,58.4 sells crawlers and the recipe) whenever this chapter has you in the harbor, and bank the Raw Mithril Head Trout; a stack of 20 is 5 hours of buff once you can cook it [G8.0,58.4 Wetlands]
At [TAR1456 Kersok Prond] (trade supplies, by the inn), [V] buy 20 Hot Spices for the omelets below (Cooking 175 takes ~30-40 of them from 150; Classic colours, unverified) [G10.4,60.6 Wetlands]
At [TAR3181 Fremal Doohickey] (First Aid trainer, in the keep), learn Heavy Wool Bandage (First Aid 115, 2 Wool Cloth each) - you should be 100-115 from the Blackrock loop; if not, make Wool at the inn first [G10.8,61.4 Wetlands]
[O]At [TAR2111 Sida], [QA470 Digging Through the Ooze] (2,400 XP) - |cffffcc00label, unknown drop rate:|r Sida's Bag drops from one of three ooze types (Black, Crimson, Monstrous: level 23-26, ~30 of them at Ironbeard's Tomb) and the DB gives no rate, so it is optional: see the ooze line after Whelgar. She takes it back at the end of chapter 19 [G11.8,58.0 Wetlands]
At [TAR2086 Valstag Ironjaw], [QA473 Report to Captain Stoutfist] (230 XP, requires level 23) [G10.1,56.9 Wetlands]
At [TAR2104 Captain Stoutfist] in the keep, [QT473] [QA464 War Banners] [QA98221 From the Ashes] [QA98230 This Land Was Their Land] [G9.9,57.5 Wetlands]
[OC]|cffffcc00Stoutfist's three are all finished in chapter 19:|r War Banners (464, 2,300 XP: 8 Dragonmaw War Banners from the Raiders, Swamprunners and Centurions of the east camps, level 26-29 and 57 Raiders in the DB, |cff66ff66normal|r - no rate listed, so keep killing as you pass), From the Ashes (98221, 2,300 XP: destroy 4 sets of Attack Plans in the Angerfang Encampment, |cff66ff66normal|r) and This Land Was Their Land (98230, 1,200 XP: only a walk to Howin Kindfeather on the east road, who then has his own quests)
At [TAR2097 Harlo Barnaby], [QA472 Fall of Dun Modr] (1,200 XP: a walk to Longbraid the Grim at Dun Modr, chapter 19; requires level 25) [G10.9,55.9 Wetlands]
At [TAR2094 James Halloran], [QA98072 Crocs of the Sky] [QA98815 Highland Hides] [QA98240 Crimson Crate Delivery] [G8.6,55.7 Wetlands]
[OC]|cffffcc00Halloran's three:|r Crocs of the Sky (98072, 2,200 XP: 8 Pristine Crimson Scales from the Red, Lost, Crimson and Flamesnorting Whelps in the hills east of the road, level 23-27, ~70 spawns, |cff66ff66normal|r - chapter 19), Highland Hides (98815, 1,150 XP: 4 Thicket Raptor Hides, dropped only by the Thicket mobs INSIDE the Excavation Site - chapter 22, a slot saver) and Crimson Crate Delivery (98240, 1,200 XP: the crate is given on accept and goes to Howin Kindfeather on the east road)
At [TAR270844 Sylessa Duskwhisper], [QA98208 Bloom of the Heavens] (2,350 XP: the flower came off the Flying Osprey) [G8.0,55.9 Wetlands]
Search the Waterlogged Chest in the wreck of the Flying Osprey at the south end of the harbor [QT321] [QA324 The Lost Ingots] [G12.1,64.2 Wetlands]
Look around the wreck for Nord'el: the DB has no coordinates for the object (item 279915), and the TUGs route collects it at the chest - |cffffcc00unverified|r [QC98208] [G12.1,64.2 Wetlands]
Kill [TAR1418 Bluegill Raider] (level 28-29, 25 of them on the beach south of the harbor) for 5 Lightforge Ingots [QC324] [G11.8,65.4 Wetlands]
[OC]|cffffcc00Label:|r Lightforge Ingots (324) - the DB lists no drop rate, but 25 raiders stand within 10 units of the chest and you need only 5; |cff66ff66normal|r
At [TAR1217 Glorin Steelbrow], [QT324] (he then offers Blessed Arm, 322 - chapter 22 takes it on its Menethil pass; the DB also lists Lightforge Ingots, 526, as a 1,750-XP alternative that excludes Blessed Arm - this guide takes Blessed Arm) [G10.6,60.6 Wetlands]
At [TAR270844 Sylessa Duskwhisper], [QT98208] [QA98209 Bloom of the Heavens] (1,200 XP: Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine, chapter 20 - the boat leaves from this harbor) [G8.0,55.9 Wetlands]
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear (98208):|r Bouquet of Auberdine Flowers (held in off-hand, +4 Sta +4 Int, fixed reward): a two-hander cannot use it, a hunter only with a one-handed melee weapon - otherwise vendor
At [TAR2096 Tarrel Rockweaver] on the road in, [QA305 In Search of The Excavation Team] (970 XP) [G11.5,52.2 Wetlands]

[OC]|cffffffffNorth bay (optional, 2,100 XP)|r  -  Apprentice's Duties (471) from chapter 09, if it is still in your log: ~30 units up the shore and the same back, with 13 level 25-26 crocs standing in the bay. If you skip it, abandon the quest [QS471]
[O]Walk north along the shore to the bay and kill [TAR2089 Giant Wetlands Crocolisk] (level 25-26, non-elite) for 6 Giant Crocolisk Skins - the DB gives no rate, 13 spawns, |cffffcc00budget ~15 kills|r [QC471] [G19.0,24.8 Wetlands]
[O]Back in Menethil at [TAR2094 James Halloran], [QT471] - |cffffcc00Gear:|r Resilient Poncho (cloak +5 Sta) if your cloak has no stats; Malleable Chain Leggings are mail: pass [G8.6,55.7 Wetlands]

[OC]|cffffffffWhelgar's Excavation Site|r  -  at the end of the road east of here (about 3 minutes). The valley is raptor country (level 22-29, non-elite), safe at 28. The Goaz Warders standing all over the dig site (55+ in the DB) are level 32 ELITES; they look like dormant statues that only wake when a Goaz Stone is used on one, but the DB does not say so: keep your distance unless you carry the stone
Follow the road east to the turn-off above the dig site [G34.1,40.8 Wetlands]
At [TAR1076 Merrin Rockweaver], [QT305] [QA306 In Search of The Excavation Team] (Merrin's Letter: back to Tarrel in Menethil, at the end of chapter 19) [G38.9,52.3 Wetlands]
At [TAR1078 Ormer Ironbraid], [QA294 Ormer's Revenge] (10 Mottled Screechers and 10 Mottled Raptors: |cff66ff66normal|r, 17 raptors and 13 screechers in the valley) [G38.2,50.9 Wetlands]
At [TAR1077 Prospector Whelgar], [QA299 Uncovering the Past] (four tablet fragments - |cff66ff66normal|r: clickable Ancient Relics and Loose Soil, 34 spots in the dig site) [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r At [TAR1077 Prospector Whelgar], [QA98216 Understanding Our Present] (3,150 XP) - the Goaz Stone he gives you wakes one Goaz Warder, a level 32 ELITE (new in Forever, no HP in the DB); the Titanic Keystone drops at 88%. Bring the tank friend [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r At [TAR1077 Prospector Whelgar], [QA98310 Gleaning Our Future] (3,200 XP) - |cffffcc00long, group only:|r a Goaz Stone for four level 32 ELITE elementals in four corners of the zone (DB spawns: Ados 77.3,47.2 east, Neru 60.2,22.1 north-east, Modr 50.6,18.9 inside Dun Modr, Golm 67.0,70.0 beside Hervdana's cave); the hearts go back to Whelgar, which chapter 22 passes again. Reward: Golem War Cloak (+6 Str, 72 armor), Rune-Etched Ring (+10 Sta) or Giantstone Medallion (+10 Spi) [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
[OC]Prospector Whelgar's Prehistoric Prism (98824) and For Further Study (98313) are chapter 22's pickups, right before the Excavation Site run
Kill [TAR1020 Mottled Raptor] and [TAR1021 Mottled Screecher] in the valley west of the dig site; Black Oozes wander among them (leave them unless you want Sida's bag) [QC294] [G24.2,48.3 Wetlands]
At [TAR1078 Ormer Ironbraid], [QT294] [QA295 Ormer's Revenge] (10 Scytheclaws and 10 Razormaws: |cff66ff66normal|r, they stand in the dig site itself) [G38.2,50.9 Wetlands]
Kill [TAR1022 Mottled Scytheclaw] and [TAR1023 Mottled Razormaw] around the dig site [QC295] [G34.1,48.2 Wetlands]
Click the Ancient Relics and Loose Soil lying around the dig site until you hold the Ados, Modr, Golm and Neru Fragments [QC299] [G34.5,47.8 Wetlands]
At [TAR1078 Ormer Ironbraid], [QT295] [QA296 Ormer's Revenge] (Sarltooth, level 29, non-elite, ~950 HP: a single kill, |cff66ff66normal|r) [G38.2,50.9 Wetlands]
[OC]Sarltooth's den lies in the south-west of the dig site; the TUGs route approaches it from the west side via 32.0,48.7 then 31.2,49.1 then 32.4,50.9 (waypoints only, unverified on Forever)
Kill [TAR1353 Sarltooth] and loot his Talon [QC296] [G33.3,51.5 Wetlands]
At [TAR1078 Ormer Ironbraid], [QT296] - learn the Recipe: Curiously Tasty Omelet (Cooking 130; Raptor Egg + Hot Spices) and cook every egg you have: it is your skill-up all the way to 175 (yellow to 170, green to 190 - Classic colours, unverified), so keep every Raptor Egg the valley and dig-site raptors drop from here on (34-40% on Wowhead Forever) [G38.2,50.9 Wetlands]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear (296):|r take |cff66ff66Raptorbane Armor|r (leather chest, 92 armor, +3 Sta, +16 Attack Power, +15 more against beasts - AP feeds Enhancement) unless your chest is better. Raptorclaw Shoulders (+3 Int, +7 spell damage) are a caster's, Excavation Rod is a wand, Raptor's End is a bow: pass
[OC][A Hunter] |cffffcc00Gear (296):|r take |cff66ff66Raptorbane Armor|r (leather chest +16 Attack Power, +15 against beasts) unless your chest is better, or |cff66ff66Raptor's End|r (bow 12.1 dps, +2 Agi +2 Sta) if your ranged weapon is weaker than that. Raptorclaw Shoulders are a caster's, Excavation Rod is a wand: pass
At [TAR1077 Prospector Whelgar], [QT299] - |cffffcc00Gear:|r Silk Mantle of Gamn (cloth shoulders +6 Int +4 Spi, fixed reward): shaman wears it only if your shoulders have no Int or Str; hunter vendors it [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]
[O]|cFFFF0000GROUP 3+|r Use the Goaz Stone next to a Goaz Warder and kill what wakes, then loot the Titanic Keystone [QC98216] [TAR270892 Goaz Warder] [G34.3,47.9 Wetlands]
[O]At [TAR1077 Prospector Whelgar], [QT98216] - |cffffcc00Gear:|r Excavation Cloak (+4 Str +4 Sta, 22 armor) unless your cloak is better; Prospector's Signet (ring +4 Sta +4 Int) only for an empty ring slot [G38.8,52.4 Wetlands]

[OC]|cffffffffLeaving Whelgar|r  -  the rest of the Wetlands is chapter 19, which starts at Howin Kindfeather on the road junction north-east of here (you walk there anyway). On the way the oozes below are optional for both of you; the shaman then has one more errand
[O]Run north to Ironbeard's Tomb and kill [TAR1032 Black Ooze] (and the Crimson and Monstrous Oozes among them, level 23-26, ~30 in all) until Sida's Bag drops - |cffffcc00unknown rate:|r give it ~10 minutes, then walk on; Sida takes the bag at the end of chapter 19, and if it never drops you can abandon her quest [QC470] [G44.8,25.5 Wetlands]
Walk on to the road junction and Howin Kindfeather's camp, where chapter 19 starts (from the Tomb the Mosshide Fenrunner camp at 45.2,34.3 lies on the way; from Whelgar go north-east) [G49.4,42.1 Wetlands]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffffffShaman side trip: Hervdana's cave|r  -  Call of Water part 4 (1,300 XP before level decay) and part 5, which hands you the Unfilled Blue Waterskin you must hold before you reach Astranaar's waters (chapter 20), so it has to happen before the boat. ~40 units south of Howin's camp, 4 minutes each way. |cffffcc00Golm|r, a level 32 ELITE elemental (his heart is quest 98310), is placed in the DB 3 units from the cave mouth (x64-69, y63-73): he may be a dormant statue like the Goaz Wardens, the DB does not say - stay west of that box until you are at the cave
[A Shaman] Walk south past the Mosshide camps toward the cave [G60.4,70.9 Wetlands]
[A Shaman] At [TAR258203 Hervdana Saegrund] in her cave under the southern falls, [QT94499] [QA94500 Call of Water] (the Blue Waterskin is filled at Astranaar; she takes it in chapter 22) [G65.8,76.4 Wetlands]
[A Shaman] Walk back north to Howin Kindfeather's camp on the road [G49.4,42.1 Wetlands]
[OC]|cffffcc00Check:|r the log should now hold, to finish in chapter 19: War Banners (464), From the Ashes (98221), This Land Was Their Land (98230), Crimson Crate Delivery (98240), Crocs of the Sky (98072), Fall of Dun Modr (472), In Search of The Excavation Team (306, for Tarrel) and Sida's bag (470) if you took it. Carried further: Bloom of the Heavens (98209, Auberdine), Highland Hides (98815, the Excavation Site), Gleaning Our Future (98310, Whelgar - if your group took it), the Gnomeregan trio (2928, 98219, 538 from the Stormwind pass) and, shaman, Call of Water (94500). Blessed Arm (322), Prehistoric Prism (98824) and For Further Study (98313) are chapter 22's pickups. Next: Howin Kindfeather and the Dragonmaw road (chapter 19)
